From: alesx2io <96351978+alesx2io@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 14:39:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] dash: open MiuiCamera directly from the lock screen

MiuiCamera handles the secure camera intent with both .Camera and
.AssistantCamera, so the lock screen shortcut asked which one to use.
Point SystemUI to com.android.camera/.Camera.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 overlay/DashSystemUIOverlay/res/values/config.xml | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/overlay/DashSystemUIOverlay/res/values/config.xml b/overlay/DashSystemUIOverlay/res/values/config.xml
index c76a902..53803fc 100644
--- a/overlay/DashSystemUIOverlay/res/values/config.xml
+++ b/overlay/DashSystemUIOverlay/res/values/config.xml
@@ -17,4 +17,9 @@
     <!-- If using proximity_sensor_type, specifies a threshold value to distinguish near and
          far break points. A sensor value less than this is considered "near". -->
     <item name="proximity_sensor_threshold" translatable="false" format="float" type="dimen">5</item>
+
+    <!-- MiuiCamera exposes both .Camera and .AssistantCamera for the secure camera intent:
+         open .Camera directly from the lock screen instead of showing a chooser. -->
+    <string name="config_cameraGesturePackage" translatable="false">com.android.camera</string>
+    <string name="config_cameraSecureActivity" translatable="false">com.android.camera/.Camera</string>
 </resources>
-- 
